Magnus Olsson (magnus@thep.lu.se) wrote:
: I've got one complaint, though: it's so slow that it's virtually
: unplayable. I tested it on a PS/2 model 70: 80386DX processor, 4 M of
: RAM, no TSR's loaded, RAMDISK option set to the correct path (and the
: ramdisk is about 2M large), DOS 3.3 (it's not my machine, and the
: owner doesn't care about upgrading). 

1) Its even a little slow, just a little on a SparcStation 2.  Which type
of binary do you have: a 8088 compatible one compiled with MicroSoft C,
or a 80386 compatible compiled with DJGPP?  The latter will allow the
game to run in the full 4MB.

2) If you are using an 8088 version, which uses overlays, then DOS 3.3
will affect its performance.  DOS 5.0 lets you free up more conventional
RAM to use on real mode programs which makes swapping of overlays less
frequent.

